{% comment %}
  Presentational, not data-shaped: it renders a single markdown *string* that
  lives at a different path in every caller.

  A scalar can't be wrapped in a `component` editable region — re-render spreads
  the object at `data-prop` as props, so the path must point at an object. The
  caller therefore passes `prop` (the path of the string, relative to the
  nearest enclosing region) and this partial emits the text region itself.
  Callers that render their own region around this omit `prop`.
{% endcomment %}
{% assign_local c = "c-text-block" %}

{% if text %}
    <div class="{{ c }}"{% if prop %} data-editable="text" data-type="block" data-prop="{{ prop }}"{% endif %}>
        {{ text | markdownify }}
    </div>
{% endif %}
